%N A398881 Number of Hausdorff set systems on an n-set with neither the empty set nor the full set.
%C A398881 A set system F on X is Hausdorff if for every two distinct elements x,y in X there exist A,B in F such that x is in A, y is in B, and A intersect B is empty.
%C A398881 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of labeled T_2-hypergraphs on n vertices without multiple edges and having neither the empty edge nor the full edge.
%H A398881 Goran Kilibarda and Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.4187">Enumeration of Certain Classes of T0-hypergraphs</a>, arXiv:1411.4187 [math.CO], 2014.
%F A398881 For a simple graph Q on [n], let D_Q be the graph whose vertices are the nonempty proper subsets of [n], with A and B adjacent iff A and B are disjoint and there exist x in A and y in B such that {x,y} is an edge of Q. Then a(n) = Sum_Q (-1)^|E(Q)| i(D_Q), where the sum is over all simple graphs Q on [n] and i(G) is the number of independent sets of G.
%e A398881 For n=3, write 1,2,3 for the singletons and 12,13,23 for the 2-subsets. The 14 Hausdorff set systems are {1,2,3}; {1,2,3,12}, {1,2,3,13}, {1,2,3,23}, {2,3,12,13}, {1,3,12,23}, {1,2,13,23}; {2,3,12,13,23}, {1,3,12,13,23}, {1,2,12,13,23}, {1,2,3,13,23}, {1,2,3,12,23}, {1,2,3,12,13}; and {1,2,3,12,13,23}. Hence a(3)=14.
%Y A398881 Cf. A326961, A059523, A059088.
